1
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:03,705
Day one. You're a waiter on a cruise ship.

2
00:00:03,755 --> 00:00:06,969
Three thousand passengers.
Seven days at sea.

3
00:00:07,169 --> 00:00:09,209
Then every phone on board buzzes at once.

4
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:10,813
Stay in your cabins.

5
00:00:11,438 --> 00:00:13,445
And the captain stops talking...

6
00:00:13,586 --> 00:00:14,942
mid-sentence.

7
00:00:15,278 --> 00:00:17,364
On Deck Five, people are
walking strangely.

8
00:00:17,414 --> 00:00:20,361
Too slowly. And they're coming this way.

9
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:23,484
Rule number one. Don't run
to the lifeboats.

10
00:00:23,534 --> 00:00:25,018
Everyone else will.

11
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,378
You go down. To the one place
nobody thinks about.

12
00:00:28,428 --> 00:00:29,633
The galley.

13
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:32,596
Food for three weeks. Water for nine days.

14
00:00:32,646 --> 00:00:34,327
And one steel door.

15
00:00:34,677 --> 00:00:37,624
Rule number two. Be quiet.
They follow sound.

16
00:00:37,867 --> 00:00:39,918
You push a cart against the door...

17
00:00:39,968 --> 00:00:41,325
and you wait.

18
00:00:45,054 --> 00:00:48,255
That night, the engines stop.
The lights stay on.

19
00:00:48,305 --> 00:00:50,044
Nobody tells you why.

20
00:00:51,182 --> 00:00:53,943
Day three. You learn the
ship's new rhythm.

21
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:58,011
Footsteps above you at noon.
Something dragging at midnight.

22
00:00:58,061 --> 00:01:00,938
And long, long silences in between.

23
00:01:01,473 --> 00:01:04,325
You ration everything. One can a day.

24
00:01:04,375 --> 00:01:09,250
Half a bottle of water. And a mark on the wall
for every day you're still here.

25
00:01:10,996 --> 00:01:13,664
Day five. Someone has been
in the cold room.

26
00:01:13,799 --> 00:01:18,139
Half your bread is gone. And the infected
don't close doors behind them.

27
00:01:19,474 --> 00:01:23,164
Day seven. You wait in the dark to see
who's stealing your food.

28
00:01:30,397 --> 00:01:32,785
A flashlight. Orange coveralls.

29
00:01:32,835 --> 00:01:35,898
And on the floor...
something they dropped.

30
00:01:37,047 --> 00:01:40,691
Whoever it is... knows this ship
better than you do.

31
00:01:42,017 --> 00:01:44,453
Day nine. The last bottle of water.

32
00:01:44,585 --> 00:01:47,277
The nearest water is the ice
machine in the crew mess.

33
00:01:47,418 --> 00:01:49,668
Forty steps down a dark corridor.

34
00:01:54,918 --> 00:01:58,051
Unfortunately, the ice machine is the
loudest thing on this ship.

35
00:02:01,791 --> 00:02:03,842
On the way out, you grab one more thing.

36
00:02:03,892 --> 00:02:05,516
The lifeboat radio.

37
00:02:05,566 --> 00:02:08,420
Forty steps there. Forty steps back.

38
00:02:08,503 --> 00:02:10,649
The last twenty at a full sprint.

39
00:02:15,398 --> 00:02:17,867
This is the Coast Guard on
channel sixteen.

40
00:02:17,917 --> 00:02:22,175
All ports are closed. Any vessel carrying
infected will not be allowed to reach

41
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:24,800
the coast. We will use force.

42
00:02:26,141 --> 00:02:29,088
That night, the speakers in the
ceiling click on.

43
00:02:32,432 --> 00:02:34,530
Nobody speaks. Someone is just...

44
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:36,958
listening. Then they click off.

45
00:02:38,290 --> 00:02:40,993
Day twelve. Through the porthole...

46
00:02:41,204 --> 00:02:46,067
a light. A lighthouse. The ship
has drifted toward land.

47
00:02:48,813 --> 00:02:51,899
Then, deep below you... the
engines start again.

48
00:02:54,634 --> 00:02:56,977
And the ship turns away from land.

49
00:02:59,324 --> 00:03:01,248
Someone else is alive on this ship.

50
00:03:01,298 --> 00:03:03,432
And they don't want to be rescued.

51
00:03:05,564 --> 00:03:07,372
You could stay in the galley. Safe.

52
00:03:07,422 --> 00:03:09,161
Fed. And blind.

53
00:03:09,308 --> 00:03:11,512
Or you could find out who's driving.

54
00:03:13,741 --> 00:03:16,653
The hatch in the cold room opens
onto a service tunnel.

55
00:03:16,736 --> 00:03:19,382
Two hundred feet of steel. No lights.

56
00:03:21,122 --> 00:03:24,580
Halfway down, you stop. Something
behind you stops too.

57
00:03:27,809 --> 00:03:31,453
You wind the kitchen timer... and
slide it into a side duct.

58
00:03:35,679 --> 00:03:37,929
Rule number two works both ways.

59
00:03:40,664 --> 00:03:43,064
Don't move. Hands where I can see them.

60
00:03:43,114 --> 00:03:44,308
Both of them.

61
00:03:45,434 --> 00:03:46,849
Where did you get that?

62
00:03:48,383 --> 00:03:51,562
You're the waiter. The one who
hums when he's scared.

63
00:03:51,709 --> 00:03:54,145
Turns out you weren't as
quiet as you thought.

64
00:03:54,777 --> 00:03:56,898
Day one, the bridge ordered all stop.

65
00:03:56,948 --> 00:04:00,557
Then the line went dead. Nobody's
opened that door since.

66
00:04:00,789 --> 00:04:03,305
Then the Coast Guard started
sinking ships.

67
00:04:03,355 --> 00:04:05,836
So every time we drift too
close to land...

68
00:04:05,886 --> 00:04:08,380
I start the engines and take us back out.

69
00:04:09,129 --> 00:04:11,285
So that's who's driving. Not a ghost.

70
00:04:11,335 --> 00:04:13,191
A very tired engineer.

71
00:04:13,517 --> 00:04:16,114
My shift ended at eight a.m. on day one.

72
00:04:16,164 --> 00:04:17,997
I just never clocked out.

73
00:04:20,123 --> 00:04:21,965
I can keep us away from the coast.

74
00:04:22,015 --> 00:04:23,767
I can't keep us fed.

75
00:04:23,992 --> 00:04:26,893
Two survivors. One kitchen.
One engine room.

76
00:04:27,031 --> 00:04:29,932
She keeps the ship alive.
You keep her fed.

77
00:04:31,669 --> 00:04:35,137
Day seventeen. You finally ask
her about the speakers.

78
00:04:35,187 --> 00:04:37,402
The click. The breathing.

79
00:04:37,929 --> 00:04:40,294
Only one place on this ship
can open the PA.

80
00:04:40,344 --> 00:04:41,480
The bridge.

81
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:45,198
It has its own water tank. The
captain's pantry.

82
00:04:45,248 --> 00:04:48,032
Enough for one person... for a month.

83
00:04:48,967 --> 00:04:53,029
One person. Thirty days. You decide
not to think about that.

84
00:04:53,255 --> 00:04:55,088
Good plan. Neither do I.

85
00:04:57,222 --> 00:04:59,890
Day twenty. A gray ship on the horizon.

86
00:05:00,226 --> 00:05:03,080
Coast Guard. Kill the lights. All of them.

87
00:05:06,812 --> 00:05:09,525
Unidentified vessel, you are
inside a closed zone.

88
00:05:09,575 --> 00:05:12,128
Turn around, or we will open fire.

89
00:05:14,853 --> 00:05:19,147
For one long hour, a ship the size of a
small town pretends it isn't there.

90
00:05:21,376 --> 00:05:23,905
Then Rosa turns it around. Again.

91
00:05:25,849 --> 00:05:30,189
Day twenty-four. The timer in the duct
stopped ringing a long time ago.

92
00:05:30,524 --> 00:05:32,182
And the thing that followed it...

93
00:05:32,393 --> 00:05:34,168
just found the way out.

94
00:05:36,894 --> 00:05:38,448
Don't. Move.

95
00:05:39,174 --> 00:05:42,678
Sound brought it here. Sound can
take it somewhere else.

96
00:05:43,013 --> 00:05:45,262
One frying pan. One empty storeroom.

97
00:05:45,312 --> 00:05:47,028
One very loud dinner bell.

98
00:05:53,774 --> 00:05:55,281
Not bad, waiter.

99
00:05:57,028 --> 00:05:59,754
Day twenty-six. She teaches
you the engines.

100
00:05:59,896 --> 00:06:02,808
You teach her that canned
peaches count as dessert.

101
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:09,041
Day twenty-nine. Fuel for one more day.

102
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:12,830
Tomorrow we pick a direction. And
we don't come back.

103
00:06:17,070 --> 00:06:18,438
That's not me.

104
00:06:18,567 --> 00:06:20,632
Steering just switched to the bridge.

105
00:06:20,715 --> 00:06:23,093
Nobody's been up there in thirty days.

106
00:06:30,825 --> 00:06:33,122
Engine room. This is the bridge.

107
00:06:33,463 --> 00:06:35,120
Thank you for keeping us alive.

108
00:06:35,170 --> 00:06:36,642
I'll take it from here.

109
00:06:38,888 --> 00:06:40,488
That's not the captain.

110
00:06:43,221 --> 00:06:47,076
Thirty days. You survived the
outbreak, the hunger and the sea.

111
00:06:47,126 --> 00:06:51,186
You found out who was driving. Now you just
have to find out where he's taking

112
00:06:51,236 --> 00:06:51,977
you.
